TITLE:: DebounceCounter
summary:: A  function debounce counter. good for double click detection
categories:: Utilities
related:: jostMlib


DESCRIPTION::
A debounce counter for functions. Has an option to fire immediately.
The mouseDownAction  of View conains a clickCount, but it is currently useless, because
its interval between clicks is much too long. Unless you wait several seconds, you always get a double click.
You can use DebounceCounter to only execute the funcition every nth time within a certain period.
This means you can use mouseUpAction too, which has no clickCount, and is much better for use in lists or TreeViews.
See the example below.  You can use it for other things too, of course, like for games.


CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
defaults are set for double-click detection

returns:: a DebounceCounter


INSTANCEMETHODS::


METHOD:: reset
resets the counter to 0


METHOD:: trigger
triggers the function after counter attempts within the wait period

PRIVATE:: prInitCount



EXAMPLES::

code::
// Test DebounceCounter
(
var dbc = DebounceCounter({ "DebounceCounter fired".postln; });
Routine({
    dbc.trigger;
    // should not fire
    0.4.wait;
    dbc.trigger;
    // should fire on second trigger
}).play;
)

(
var dbc = DebounceCounter({ "DebounceCounter different args - should not fire".postln; });
dbc.trigger("a");
dbc.trigger("b");
// should not fire since args differ...
// NOTE: this only works if you add an equality check in the class
)

(
var dbc = DebounceCounter({ "DebounceCounter reset - should not fire".postln; });
dbc.trigger;
dbc.reset;
dbc.trigger;
// should not fire, count resets
)

(
var dbc = DebounceCounter({ |txt| ("DebounceCounter arg passed:" + txt).postln; });
Routine({
    dbc.trigger("hello");
    0.4.wait;
    dbc.trigger("hello");
}).play;
// should print "hello"
)

// A double click detector might look like this:
v=TreeView.new;
// ... add items

var dbc = DebounceCounter({ |item|
    item.postln;
});

v.mouseUpAction_({ |tr| // do NOT use mouseDownAction here.  It won't  know which item was selected in time.
    dbc.trigger(tr.currentItem.strings[1]);
});

// will only trigger dbc on double click.

::
